node_modules

.vercel
# Blanket rule, kept narrow on purpose. `.env*` here would also swallow .env.example, which is
# meant to be committed: it is the setup reference (placeholder values only) that a fresh clone
# reads before creating .env.local. Real secrets are already excluded by the explicit rules
# above, so the wildcard buys nothing and cost this file its tracking.
.env*
!.env.example
